rota lap 5223, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes; read up close and RUN the actual thing. The row's fixed seat claims the happy zone proved the whole drain, so caravan_drain_replay_witness was run rather than cited: GREEN, seven asks on three rings, four region stores byte-identical. Its sibling claim about the choir is the find below.
think Water's sense pointed the whole lap: the foundation's citations were resolved by hand rather than trusted, and the class that turned up was the citations themselves.
think A Markdown link makes two promises and both are held -- tracked_link_scan gates the target, link_text_promise_scan walls the anchor text at zero. A path in bare backticks with no link around it is read by neither, and it is the shape this tree writes most: a Kin line, a Machinery line, a table cell.
think The recognition rule was already ours. tools/hooks/commit-msg has refused this exact shape in a commit body since REDS %202 -- a slash, an extension this tree writes, asked of the filesystem -- so the promise was checked where it can never be edited and unchecked where it can.
think First measurement read 758 hits across 300 pages, and most were false. Excluding testimony rooms, the two append-only ledgers, link anchor text and placeholder shapes brought it to 71.
think Then one page taught a third spelling. classical-vedic-astrology/templates/reading-template.md writes studies/life-frame/... in a table cell and links ../studies/life-frame/... one line above; both are honest to a reader standing in that room. Reading root and page relative alone counted 60 of its cells as broken promises.
think A fourth class was built and then dropped for being unmeasurable. A room this tree holds untracked on purpose looked worth counting apart, and git check-ignore -v .lap/msg.txt answers .gitignore:8:/* -- exactly what it answers for old/doc/spec/flw.txt, another project's file. On a deny-by-default tree that question reads is this allow-listed, so the split went and those citations stay counted.
obs The reading is a ratchet at 65 rather than a wall, because each hit wants the lane that owns its page -- four name docs/TIGER_STYLE.md, six the work-in-progress room breached to crux a month ago, and context/TAME_GUIDANCE.md cites tools/foo.rish.
obs A find named rather than taken: caravan_suite_witness went RED on its first rung, tools/ca/caravan_ladder_spine_witness.rish, while a stale roster pass held this tree's build lock. That witness runs GREEN standalone, so the reading is flaky under contention rather than a confirmed red, and it is Caravan's lane. Not booked; named here and on the card.
obs Two finds named rather than taken. The cold endurance run reddened ryekey, which answers ryekey_verdict=machine_fact and asks for a rebuild after a peer moved ryekey_marker to v9 -- and the witness then stops at an UnknownStatement on line 55 of tools/r/ryekey_witness.rish, so it cannot finish either way. Bakery's lane.
obs The hot endurance run reddened the guard on its own seating lap, and it was right. This round's own account quoted three broken citations as evidence and the scan counted all three, 65 to 68 -- the shape derived-spine already names for pen plants, where a meter reading for truth hears a sentence that must stay false exactly as it hears one asserting it. The examples are described in prose now and spelled only in the scan's listing; the lesson is in the scan's own header.
obs The hot run also reddened fold_shelf_link_repoint on the new shelf page: a link carried down from the card kept the card's depth. tools/f/fold_shelf_link_repoint.sh --apply computed and made the one repair, and both guards read GREEN afterward.
obs The commit-msg path wall refused this round's own body three times, for naming the broken citations the round exists to count. Quoting a stale path as evidence and asserting it as a reference are two different acts and the guard reads one shape, which is the standing ask the card already carries one lane over.
